Music data licensing
====================

Open Opus metadata: public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal.
Publisher declaration: https://www.openopus.org/
Publisher repository declaration: https://github.com/openopus-org/openopus_api#license
CC0 terms: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
Dataset: https://api.openopus.org/work/dump.json
Snapshot 2026-10-13, SHA256 6e610314c613eba428907a790ffb632446322439c0c2b526305e06d113ca164f.
Open Opus's GPLv3 API software is not included.

Corpora instrument names: CC0 1.0 Universal.
Darius Kazemi and Corpora contributors.
https://github.com/dariusk/corpora/tree/2e7adec11a0561696c236ae1fca82e88be173d42
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dariusk/corpora/2e7adec11a0561696c236ae1fca82e88be173d42/README.md
CC0 terms: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
Original names transformed, sound-mechanism framing added, two spelling
corrections applied, two piano-size duplicates omitted. See README.md.

Historical Billboard chart records reproduce factual metadata with original
framing. No lyrics, recordings, images, reviews or Wikipedia prose are included.
See record provenance for the exact source revision and verification limitation.

Generator code and original generated musical artifacts are authored for
Inspire and follow the project's licensing. No external melodies are copied.
